ako","H3290","HNpm","Jacob"],["לְצַוֹּת","letzavot","H6680","HR/Vpcc","to command"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["בָּנָיו","banav","H1121","HNcmpc/Sp3ms","sons his"],["וַיֶּאֱסֹף","vaiye'esof","H622","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he gathered"],["רַגְלָיו","raglav","H7272","HNcfdc/Sp3ms","feet his"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","into"],["הַמִּטָּה","hamitah","H4296","HTd/Ncfsa","the bed"],["וַיִּגְוַע","vaiyigva'","H1478","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he expired"],["וַיֵּאָסֶף","vaiye'asef","H622","Hc/VNw3ms","and he was gathered"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["עַמָּיו","'amav","H5971","HNcmpc/Sp3ms","peoples his"]],"x":[[1049029,1049029,6],[1025008,1025008,4],[1035029,1035029,3]],"xn":3}},"people":[{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[1,2,7,16,24,28,33]},{"id":"reuben_2429","name":"Reuben","also":"","summary":"Behold a son!, the eldest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 29:32). His sinful conduct, referred to in Gen. 35:22, brought down upon him his dying father’s malediction (48:4).","verses":70,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[3]},{"id":"levi_1820","name":"Levi","also":"","summary":"The third son of Jacob by Leah. The origin of the name is found in Leah’s words (Gen. 29:34), “This time will my husband be joined [Heb. yillaveh] unto me.”","verses":64,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[5]},{"id":"simeon_2741","name":"Simeon","also":"","summary":"The second son of Jacob by Leah (Gen. 29:33). He was associated with Levi in the terrible act of vengeance against Hamor and the Shechemites (34:25, 26).","verses":40,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[5]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[8,9,10]},{"id":"jesus_905","name":"Jesus","also":"Immanuel, Emmanuel, Messiah, Shiloh, Christ, Jesus Christ, Messias","summary":"Anointed, the Greek translation of the Hebrew word rendered “Messiah”, the official title of our Lord, occurring five hundred and fourteen times in the New Testament.","verses":1831,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Mary","v":[10]},{"id":"zebulun_3002","name":"Zebulun","also":"Zabulon","summary":"Dwelling, the sixth and youngest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 30:20). Little is known of his personal history.","verses":46,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[13]},{"id":"issachar_645","name":"Issachar","also":"","summary":"Hired (Gen. 30:18). “God hath given me,” said Leah, “my hire (Heb. sekhari)...and she called his name Issachar.” He was Jacob’s ninth son, and was born in Padan-aram (comp. 28:2).","verses":38,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[14]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[16,17]},{"id":"gad_1262","name":"Gad","also":"","summary":"Jacob’s seventh son, by Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid, and the brother of Asher (Gen. 30:11-13; 46:16, 18).","verses":55,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[19]},{"id":"asher_337","name":"Asher","also":"Aser","summary":"Happy, Jacob’s eigth son; his mother was Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid (Gen. 30:13). Of the tribe founded by him nothing is recorded beyond its holding a place in the list of the tribes (35:26; 46:17; Ex. 1:4, etc.) It increased in numbers twenty-nine percent, during the thirty-eight years’ wanderings.","verses":43,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[20]},{"id":"naphtali_2149","name":"Naphtali","also":"Nephthalim","summary":"My wrestling, the fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s handmaid (Gen. 30:8). When Jacob went down into Egypt, Naphtali had four sons (Gen. 46:24).","verses":49,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[21]},{"id":"joseph_1710","name":"Joseph","also":"Zaphnath-paaneah","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 30:23, 24), who, on the occasion of his birth, said, “God hath taken away [Heb. ‘asaph] my reproach.”","verses":199,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[22,26]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[27]},{"id":"ephron_1208","name":"Ephron","also":"","summary":"The son of Zohar a Hittite, the owner of the field and cave of Machpelah, which Abraham bought for 400 shekels of silver (Gen. 23:8-17; 25:9; 49:29, 30).","verses":10,"father":"Zohar","mother":"","v":[29,30]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[30,31]},{"id":"canaan_914","name":"Canaan","also":"Canaanites, Canaanite","summary":"The fourth son of Ham (Gen. 10:6). His descendants were under a curse in consequence of the transgression of his father (9:22-27). His eldest son, Zidon, was the father of the Sidonians and Phoenicians.","verses":84,"father":"Ham","mother":"","v":[30]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[31]},{"id":"sarah_2473","name":"Sarah","also":"Sarai, Sara","summary":"Princess, the wife and at the same time the half-sister of Abraham (Gen. 11:29; 20:12). This name was given to her at the time that it was announced to Abraham that she should be the mother of the promised child.","verses":48,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[31]},{"id":"leah_1813","name":"Leah","also":"","summary":"Weary, the eldest daughter of Laban, and sister of Rachel (Gen. 29:16). Jacob took her to wife through a deceit of her father (Gen. 29:23). She was “tender-eyed” (17).","verses":32,"father":"Laban","mother":"","v":[31]},{"id":"rebekah_2401","name":"Rebekah","also":"","summary":"A noose, the daughter of Bethuel, and the wife of Isaac (Gen. 22:23; 24:67). The circumstances under which Abraham’s “steward” found her at the “city of Nahor,” in Padan-aram, are narrated in Gen. 24-27.","verses":29,"father":"Bethuel","mother":"","v":[31]},{"id":"heth_1510","name":"Heth","also":"","summary":"Dread, a descendant of Canaan, and the ancestor of the Hittites (Gen. 10:18; Deut. 7:1), who dwelt in the vicinity of Hebron (Gen. 23:3, 7).","verses":12,"father":"Canaan","mother":"","v":[32]}],"places":[{"id":"sidon_1093","name":"Sidon","kind":"City","lat":33.56024,"lon":35.37121,"summary":"A fishery, a town on the Mediterranean coast, about 25 miles north of Tyre. It received its name from the “first-born” of Canaan, the grandson of Noah (Gen. 10:15, 19).","verses":30,"v":[13]},{"id":"zebulun_1289","name":"Zebulun","kind":"Region","lat":32.71486,"lon":35.23957,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1266 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":16,"v":[13]},{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[30]},{"id":"machpelah_748","name":"Machpelah","kind":"Landmark (Cave)","lat":31.52465,"lon":35.11073,"summary":"Portion; double cave, the cave which Abraham bought, together with the field in which it stood, from Ephron the Hittite, for a family burying-place (Gen. 23).","verses":6,"v":[30]},{"id":"mamre_762","name":"Mamre","kind":"","lat":31.5491,"lon":35.09356,"summary":"The name of the place in the neighbourhood of Hebron where Abraham dwelt (Gen. 23:17, 19; 35:27); called also in Authorized Version (13:18) the “plain of Mamre,” but in Revised Version more correctly “the oaks [marg., ‘terebinths’] of Mamre.”","verses":6,"v":[30]}],"events":[{"id":"death_of_jacob_116","title":"Death of Jacob","year":-1689,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 47:28–49:31. People: Israel. Place: Egypt.","v":[28,29,30,31]},{"id":"lifetime_of_jacob_86","title":"Lifetime of Jacob","year":-1836,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 25:24–49:33. People: Israel. Lasted about 180 years.","v":[33]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3290,3290,7121,7121,1121,1121,559,559,622,622,5046,5046,5046,5046,5046,0,834,7122,7122,853,853,3117,3117,3117,319,319],[6908,6908,8085,8085,1121,1121,3290,3290,8085,413,1,1,3478],[7205,859,1060,1060,1060,3581,3581,7225,7225,7225,202,202,202,3499,7613,7613,3499,5794,5794],[6349,4325,4325,4325,408,408,408,3498,3498,3588,5927,5927,5927,1,1,1,4904,5927,3326,3326,227,2490,2490],[8095,3878,3878,251,251,4380,4380,3627,3627,2555,2555],[5315,5315,408,935,5475,5475,3519,3519,408,3161,6951,6951,3588,2026,2026,376,639,639,639,6131,6131,7794,7522,7522,7522],[779,779,639,639,3588,5794,5794,5794,5678,5678,5678,3588,7185,7185,7185,2505,2505,2505,2505,3290,3290,6327,6327,6327,3478,3478],[3063,251,251,3034,3034,3034,3027,3027,6203,6203,6203,6203,6203,341,341,341,1,1,1121,7812,7812,7812,0,0],[3063,1482,1482,1482,738,1121,5927,5927,2964,2964,2964,738,738,738,3766,3766,7257,7257,7257,3833,3833,3833,4310,6965,6965,6965,6965],[7626,7626,3808,3808,5493,3063,3063,2710,2710,2710,996,996,7272,7272,5704,7886,935,3349,3349,3349,5971,5971,5971,0,0],[631,631,5895,5895,1612,1612,1612,1121,1121,8321,8321,8321,8321,3526,3526,3830,3830,3196,3196,5497,5497,1818,1818,1818,6025,6025],[5869,5869,2447,2447,3196,3196,8127,8127,8127,3836,3836,2461,2461],[2074,7931